# db-combolite C99 formatting — shared across packages, calibrated to the existing tree (do not
# reformat wholesale; CI runs `clang-format --dry-run -Werror` on changed lines). See CLAUDE.md.
# A small amount of intentional hand-formatting (packed byte-tables, grouped short assignments) is
# guarded with `// clang-format off` / `// clang-format on`.
---
Language: Cpp
BasedOnStyle: LLVM
IndentWidth: 4
TabWidth: 4
UseTab: Never
ColumnLimit: 100
PointerAlignment: Right
DerivePointerAlignment: false
BreakBeforeBraces: Linux
BreakBeforeBinaryOperators: NonAssignment
AllowShortFunctionsOnASingleLine: None
AllowShortIfStatementsOnASingleLine: Never
AllowShortLoopsOnASingleLine: false
AllowShortCaseLabelsOnASingleLine: true
AlignAfterOpenBracket: Align
AlignEscapedNewlines: Left
SortIncludes: false
KeepEmptyLinesAtTheStartOfBlocks: false
SpaceAfterCStyleCast: false
...
